00:15:34,180 --> 00:15:35,680
She was my only girl.

261
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:39,220
It was this past September
that she turned 17.

262
00:15:40,740 --> 00:15:42,640
Please, forgive me for asking,

263
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:47,371
but I would much prefer it if we could
continue our conversation in private.

264
00:15:47,660 --> 00:15:49,895
While I am sympathetic to your plight,

265
00:15:50,140 --> 00:15:54,846
the men in this room place their absolute
trust in me, and I place mine in them.

266
00:15:55,020 --> 00:16:00,000
So unfortunately, I can't just ask them to
simply interrupt their meal for our sake.

267
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:01,960
That would be plain rude.

268
00:16:04,980 --> 00:16:07,600
It all happened suddenly a few months ago.

269
00:16:08,200 --> 00:16:12,906
I learned from my wife that our daughter
had gone and found herself a boyfriend.

270
00:16:13,940 --> 00:16:17,497
She told me the young man was a
sculptor just beginning on his way,

271
00:16:17,580 --> 00:16:19,286
but that didn't matter to me.

272
00:16:19,580 --> 00:16:22,639
I didn't even mind that he
was a bit older than her.

273
00:16:23,060 --> 00:16:26,660
Yet never, not once, did he
come to meet me and my wife.

274
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:29,120
That never sat quite right with me.

275
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:32,100
Then, all of a sudden,

276
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:36,737
my precious flower fell from the
roof of that man's apartment.

277
00:16:36,820 --> 00:16:39,560
clutching to her chest some strange rock.

278
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:48,480
I'm sorry.

279
00:16:48,860 --> 00:16:50,400
I've lost my composure.

280
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:54,840
Why does the pain still feel
so fresh after all this time?

281
00:16:55,160 --> 00:16:56,800
My daughter was my hope.

282
00:16:57,180 --> 00:16:58,860
She was young and beautiful.

283
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:02,660
She lit up my world with
her astounding radiance.

284
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:05,517
I beg you to do everything that you can.

285
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:07,137
To see that my girl is avenged,

286
00:17:07,220 --> 00:17:10,573
please make that rotten
scoundrel suffer for what he did.

287
00:17:11,500 --> 00:17:14,277
Stop for a moment, you
think she was killed?

288
00:17:14,360 --> 00:17:15,777
Am I hearing you correctly?

289
00:17:15,860 --> 00:17:18,597
And you believe this
boyfriend was the killer?

290
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:20,737
That he was the one who
pushed her off of the roof?

291
00:17:20,820 --> 00:17:23,057
I must say I find this quite strange.

292
00:17:23,140 --> 00:17:25,957
News of murder in this
town always reaches me.

293
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:28,717
The police refused to
start an investigation.

294
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:33,317
They wrote it off as suicide and
swept the case aside like my lawyer.

295
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:37,580
But as Sir Family, we can
swear to you one thing.

296
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:41,780
Our beautiful girl would
never have taken her own life.

297
00:17:42,780 --> 00:17:45,956
Both my wife and I know this
to be true in our hearts.

298
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:47,296
You're my last hope.

299
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:50,257
There's nobody else left I
can turn to at this point.

300
00:17:50,340 --> 00:17:53,757
I ask you to make that bastard
feel just a fraction of my pain.

301
00:17:53,840 --> 00:17:55,557
Let him have a small taste of what I will

302
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:58,117
endure for the remainder
of my wretched life.

303
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:01,840
I'm sorry this world has been
cruel to you, but I can't help.

304
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:04,746
I'm afraid my condolences
are all I can offer.

305
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:08,977
Don't mistake us for a band of lowly
ruffians who would kill anyone for money!

306
00:18:09,060 --> 00:18:12,137
But I've seen the things you've
done for the people in town!

307
00:18:12,220 --> 00:18:15,397
All I'm really asking for is
justice for my departed daughter?

308
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:17,520
You say you want justice?

309
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:21,897
Signore, not long ago you wished
to speak together in private?

310
00:18:21,980 --> 00:18:23,577
And I've figured out why!

311
00:18:23,660 --> 00:18:28,100
It seems you are perfectly aware
of how dangerous your inquiry is.

312
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:34,540
Still, I'll admit your devotion to
your Family struck a chord with me.

313
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:37,280
It's one of my soft spots.

314
00:18:38,220 --> 00:18:39,860
In addition to all that,

315
00:18:40,080 --> 00:18:43,897
I also think it's rather suspicious that
no one else has been moved by your story.

316
00:18:43,980 --> 00:18:47,037
This might just be worth
looking into after all!

317
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:52,017
I suppose at least, we'll see what
this mysterious sculptor has to say.

318
00:18:52,100 --> 00:18:55,865
I will ask for your payment only
after he has been found guilty.

319
00:18:57,080 --> 00:18:58,260
Do you accept?

320
00:19:00,280 --> 00:19:02,220
God bless your soul, signore.

321
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:07,699
Mister, I would like to
take you on this assignment.

322
00:19:08,260 --> 00:19:09,090
Sounds good.

323
00:19:13,180 --> 00:19:14,400
What the hell?

324
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:16,380
Did I lay this thing?

325
00:19:26,560 --> 00:19:29,640
Mista, be sure to put that
back where you found it.

326
00:19:30,420 --> 00:19:31,417
Did I just…

327
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:32,680
did I knock it over?

328
00:19:32,940 --> 00:19:35,037
Do you know where this
stone was perched earlier?

329
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:37,717
Because I swear it's almost
like it popped out of the air.

330
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:39,837
Just watch yourself
when you're standing up.

331
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:42,720
I prefer my things not
in pieces on the ground.

332
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:47,057
Mista, Bucciarati says he'll
give you a ride part of the way.

333
00:19:47,140 --> 00:19:47,970
Right.

334
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:54,890
Take this.

335
00:19:54,973 --> 00:19:59,488
I've written down the sculptor's home
address and here's a picture of our man!

336
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,257
Have a little chat with him.

337
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:02,497
See what you can find out.

338
00:20:02,580 --> 00:20:07,637
You're free to employ physical coercion
if you need to get a clear confession.

339
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:09,957
You have your recorder. Yeah.

340
00:20:10,040 --> 00:20:13,477
But just so I know, how far is too far?

341
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:16,997
Like if it turns out he did
push that poor girl off a roof,

342
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:18,897
how many bullets am I supposed to use?

343
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:20,837
Remember we're not assassins.

344
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:23,657
Let's just put him in a wheelchair
for the rest of the decade.

345
00:20:23,740 --> 00:20:25,457
The police can take it from there.

346
00:20:25,540 --> 00:20:29,011
That should be more than enough
to cool the old man's rage!

347
00:20:35,960 --> 00:20:36,790
Hey.

348
00:20:36,873 --> 00:20:37,703
Where you off to?

349
00:20:37,786 --> 00:20:38,957
Will you stop messing around?

350
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:39,981
We'll leave you.

351
00:20:43,620 --> 00:20:46,520
Mista, what's the damn
holdup? Need a shit?

352
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:47,700
Just wait a sec.

353
00:20:47,860 --> 00:20:49,978
I'm doing something important, okay?

354
00:20:52,740 --> 00:20:54,820
You look troubled. What's wrong?

355
00:20:55,340 --> 00:20:56,170
Well,

356
00:20:56,253 --> 00:20:58,157
there's something about
that old man's story

357
00:20:58,240 --> 00:21:00,777
that's rubbing me wrong all
sorts of ways right now.

358
00:21:00,860 --> 00:21:02,337
Like when his daughter fell.

359
00:21:02,420 --> 00:21:03,557
If I'm remembering right,

360
00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:06,837
he mentioned something about her
clutching a weird stone of some sort.

361
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:09,567
Did he say exactly what
kind of stone it was?

362
00:21:10,260 --> 00:21:11,090
No.

363
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:13,157
Wait, he said nothing about its shape?

364
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:14,660
Or even how big it was?

365
00:21:14,840 --> 00:21:18,037
I mean, the freaking dude is
a sculptor, for God's sake.

366
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:19,897
All he said was it looked strange.

367
00:21:19,980 --> 00:21:21,000
Not much else.

368
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:22,660
Ah, son of a bitch!

369
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:26,157
I could name a ton of different
things that look strange.

370
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:29,237
Unfortunately, it was the
only adjective he gave us.

371
00:21:29,320 --> 00:21:30,377
What's on your mind?

372
00:21:30,460 --> 00:21:31,342
This is sudden.

373
00:21:34,020 --> 00:21:35,700
Wait, it's the stone!

374
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:44,940
Hey, pull over for a
sec, Fugo! Stop the car!

375
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:46,570
For what?

376
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:48,092
Slam the brakes, dammit!

377
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:53,571
Hey, man, I told you to go before we left.

378
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:56,360
Uh, yeah. Never mind.

379
00:21:56,660 --> 00:21:57,917
Thought I saw something.

380
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:58,830
My bad.

381
00:21:59,020 --> 00:22:00,457
Just forget I said anything.

382
00:22:00,540 --> 00:22:01,716
Are you okay, Mista?

383
00:22:02,140 --> 00:22:04,677
I mean, how much wine
did you have to drink?

384
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:07,525
Hey, why is that always
the first place you go?

385
00:22:07,700 --> 00:22:08,876
I'm not drunk, okay?

386
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:10,235
Maybe a little loopy.

387
00:22:10,420 --> 00:22:11,957
Think before you speak, man.

388
00:22:12,040 --> 00:22:13,511
Words can hurt, you know?

389
00:22:14,260 --> 00:22:16,084
Wait, isn't that it over there?

390
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:17,534
All right, let me out.

391
00:22:20,960 --> 00:22:22,500
Jeez, what a drama queen.

392
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:24,200
I feel bad for him.

393
00:22:24,380 --> 00:22:28,317
Not sure he really wants a friend right
now, but maybe I should just go with him.

394
00:22:28,400 --> 00:22:29,230
It's fine.

395
00:22:29,313 --> 00:22:30,651
I can watch Mista's back.

396
00:22:32,440 --> 00:22:34,616
Better to err on the side of caution.

397
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:38,682
Those rumors of stand users convening
on our city has me on guard.

398
00:22:39,580 --> 00:22:41,440
Go look into Leaky Eye Leaky.

399
00:22:41,820 --> 00:22:42,879
You got it, Chief.

400
00:22:47,380 --> 00:22:49,840
So, the guy lives on the seventh floor.

401
00:22:50,080 --> 00:22:51,920
And right above it is the roof.

402
00:22:52,200 --> 00:22:53,780
Nice place, Skolipi.

403
00:22:57,540 --> 00:22:58,857
And there's the courtyard.

404
00:22:58,940 --> 00:23:02,881
That's the spot where the old man
said his daughter hit the ground.

405
00:23:22,480 --> 00:23:23,460
That's a stand!

406
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:25,211
So I wasn't seeing stuff.

407
00:23:25,480 --> 00:23:27,697
This just got a whole
lot more interesting.

408
00:23:27,780 --> 00:23:29,340
Watch out, Rock!

409
00:23:29,620 --> 00:23:31,738
I'm gonna figure out your damn deal!

410
00:23:34,980 --> 00:23:35,810
Butrati...

411
00:23:57,780 --> 00:23:59,800
Thank you.
